      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-4700",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=4 \\\\ 4x+10y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/example-4700.json",
          "file_sha256": "a5d252a64d8aa411380c1727a7cf5c2f290874e8828e3ba001d836d3591d7350"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1437,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1438
    },
    {
      "question": "e-4700",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "cd1e918c9c161a4cba64a696d069cbe1773de962370e487d1c8e592b29ef9fe2",
      "new_sha256": "0cbe2da055b371173f746441964e6c1f816bb6694c46d8a3f546a6e34af8665b",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-4700",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{5}{2}y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-8$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-8,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/example-4700.json",
          "file_sha256": "a5d252a64d8aa411380c1727a7cf5c2f290874e8828e3ba001d836d3591d7350"
        }
      ],
